{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/fixtures/plsql/constants_spec.sql@L1","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/fixtures/plsql/constants_spec.sql","span":{"start":1,"end":5}},"file":"packages/parsers/fixtures/plsql/constants_spec.sql","span":{"start":1,"end":5},"lang":"plsql","hash":"blake3:436660a1ceaf5b642aa924f56b3816366ee44f6f9d1076e906d33ea0781d886f","meta":{"text":"PL/SQL fixture for WS-6 constant-value capture: a package SPEC with CONSTANT declarations\n(the CONSTANT keyword PRECEDES the type in Oracle: `cname CONSTANT NUMBER := 30;`) plus a\nplain defaulted variable and a parameterless procedure declaration. Asserts the literal\ninitializer, the constant flag, and the CORRECT dataType (NUMBER / VARCHAR2(20), not the\nliteral string \"CONSTANT\") all survive into the package node's meta.variables."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts@L131","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":131,"end":136}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":131,"end":136},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:149133735dfdb4a1f7149cf540e4b15fa338ae4284fa2b64b65037159fcbb099","meta":{"text":"Heuristic cluster label: `\"<longestCommonDirPrefix(memberFiles)> · <dominantStereotypeOrType>\"`.\nReturns `undefined` when the members span roots (no shared directory prefix), so the caller falls\nback to the highest-degree member's qualified name. Deterministic: stereotype/type tallies use\nalphabetical tie-breaks; the directory prefix is mechanical."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts@L145","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":145,"end":146}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":145,"end":146},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3aaad5e61bc3bb9d6d84d4d2172fb4de4f226d0ddc6c7f01d466114b9052edec","meta":{"text":"Longest common leading directory prefix across a set of file paths. Returns `undefined` when\nthere is no shared first segment (members live under different roots)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts@L161","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":161,"end":162}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":161,"end":162},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:893552c12dd2600d78ec3f1e63d86d43ec63e0af75b1bd908f29370605ebd78a","meta":{"text":"The most common stereotype among the members, else the most common `type`, else `'symbol'`.\nAlphabetical tie-breaks so the label is deterministic run-to-run."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts@L184","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":184,"end":184}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/cluster/cluster.ts","span":{"start":184,"end":184},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:eca4ec529d75a55347849621e90252d70eb2a961abe91baadbe219a75c83757f","meta":{"text":"Fallback label: the highest-degree member's qualified name (the pre-E behavior)."}}
